1
00:00:01,513 --> 00:00:04,182
Oh no, I'm gonna be late!

2
00:00:04,266 --> 00:00:06,435
[Anzu] Wait. What did I just say?

3
00:00:06,518 --> 00:00:09,312
That phrase… It sounded so familiar.

4
00:00:09,396 --> 00:00:10,939
[yelps]

5
00:00:11,982 --> 00:00:13,942
[Hijiri] She's the one
who went running out into the street

6
00:00:14,025 --> 00:00:15,444
right in front of us.

7
00:00:16,862 --> 00:00:18,947
ONE WAY STREET

8
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:21,366
[officer] Please, miss,
be more aware of your surroundings.

9
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:22,409
[soft chuckle]

10
00:00:23,577 --> 00:00:25,579
[Tsuchiya]
Let us give you a ride to school.

11
00:00:27,330 --> 00:00:28,415
[car door closes]

12
00:00:30,167 --> 00:00:32,753
[Anzu]
It seems like a pretty expensive car.

13
00:00:33,503 --> 00:00:34,963
[car door closes]

14
00:00:35,046 --> 00:00:37,924
Hey, um, I'm really sorry
that I made you late.

15
00:00:38,633 --> 00:00:40,135
Having a couple of tardies?

16
00:00:40,886 --> 00:00:44,014
That won't affect my report card.
I'm an excellent student.

17
00:00:44,514 --> 00:00:47,476
[Anzu] Anyway,
why would a rich kid like him

18
00:00:47,559 --> 00:00:49,186
go to a public school?

19
00:00:49,269 --> 00:00:52,022
He's good-looking
but I haven't seen him before.

20
00:00:52,606 --> 00:00:54,441
Well, you must be ecstatic.

21
00:00:55,233 --> 00:00:58,945
I mean, getting the chance
to ride to school with me and everything.

22
00:00:59,529 --> 00:01:01,031
[Hijiri] You should be grateful.

23
00:01:01,114 --> 00:01:01,948
[grunts]

24
00:01:04,034 --> 00:01:06,870
[Anzu in deep voice] Hang on, Anzu,
don't punch him in the face.

25
00:01:06,953 --> 00:01:10,832
Hold it in. This all happened
because I was being careless.

26
00:01:12,167 --> 00:01:14,836
[in normal voice]
Oh. Both Kazuki and Saki messaged me.

27
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:15,754
TSUKASA: YOU GOOD?

28
00:01:15,837 --> 00:01:17,047
I should respond.

29
00:01:17,130 --> 00:01:19,341
I GOT IN A MINOR ACCIDENT,
BUT I'M OKAY.

30
00:01:24,137 --> 00:01:26,139
[theme music]

31
00:02:49,389 --> 00:02:50,223
[school bell dings]

32
00:02:50,307 --> 00:02:53,727
#7: WHAT A STRONG PERSONALITY

33
00:02:53,810 --> 00:02:56,313
[indistinct chatter]

34
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:58,857
[Anzu] Great, just in time for break.

35
00:03:01,234 --> 00:03:03,820
Uh, this is me right here.

36
00:03:04,404 --> 00:03:06,865
[Hijiri] You exchanged contacts
with Tsuchiya, right?

37
00:03:06,948 --> 00:03:07,782
Hmm?

38
00:03:07,866 --> 00:03:09,910
-[Tsuchiya] My name is Tsuchiya.
-Oh, yeah.

39
00:03:10,410 --> 00:03:13,330
[Hijiri] I'll be in touch at a later day.
You just wait.

40
00:03:14,247 --> 00:03:16,207
And enjoy dreaming about me.

41
00:03:17,918 --> 00:03:20,420
[Anzu] Seriously?
There's still more to talk about?

42
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:23,673
-Hmm?
-[gasps]

43
00:03:23,757 --> 00:03:24,591
Oh…

44
00:03:24,674 --> 00:03:28,345
Anzu! Why did you arrive
with Mr. Hijiri Koganei?

45
00:03:28,428 --> 00:03:29,262
Mister?

46
00:03:29,346 --> 00:03:31,848
Anzu, are… are you sure
that you're not hurt?

47
00:03:31,932 --> 00:03:33,266
Yeah, thank you, Saki.

48
00:03:33,350 --> 00:03:35,310
[gasps]
You are so lucky!

49
00:03:35,393 --> 00:03:38,021
-[exclaims]
-You got hit by Mr. Hijiri's car.

50
00:03:38,104 --> 00:03:39,773
[Anzu] Why do you keep saying "Mister"?

51
00:03:39,856 --> 00:03:40,774
What do you mean?

52
00:03:40,857 --> 00:03:43,735
He's Mr. Hijiri Koganei,
the rich star from Class 8!

53
00:03:43,818 --> 00:03:46,112
He is like a prince.
He even has his own fan club.

54
00:03:46,196 --> 00:03:47,030
PRINCE HIJIRI

55
00:03:47,739 --> 00:03:48,865
I see…

56
00:03:49,366 --> 00:03:51,034
[Anzu] I mean, it seems obvious,

57
00:03:51,117 --> 00:03:54,537
but, this has got to be
another one of their setups!

58
00:03:54,621 --> 00:03:56,498
-[Anzu] I got to get up…
-And insert!

59
00:03:56,581 --> 00:03:59,417
-[Anzu] I'll be late…
-Now she'll be running really late!

60
00:03:59,501 --> 00:04:00,835
-[Makoto] Hosshi!
-[Junta] Anzu!

61
00:04:00,919 --> 00:04:02,045
Oh!

62
00:04:02,128 --> 00:04:05,131
-Are you okay? We heard you got hit!
-Anzu, I was worried about you.

63
00:04:06,132 --> 00:04:07,425
[in high-pitched voice]
Hayami! Oh gosh!

64
00:04:07,509 --> 00:04:10,512
-You're not hurt at all, are you?
-Nope. I'm all good.

65
00:04:11,096 --> 00:04:12,138
[sighs]

66
00:04:13,056 --> 00:04:15,558
I bet you were rushing
and ran into the street.

67
00:04:15,642 --> 00:04:16,768
Yeah.

68
00:04:16,851 --> 00:04:19,479
Still, I really think
you should go to the hospital.

69
00:04:19,562 --> 00:04:21,231
The car barely hit me, though.

70
00:04:21,314 --> 00:04:23,483
Hosshi, you and Hayami are friends?

71
00:04:23,566 --> 00:04:24,901
Nice!

72
00:04:24,985 --> 00:04:27,946
He's, um, he's an "old friend,"
quote unquote.

73
00:04:28,029 --> 00:04:29,364
-Let's go.
-[squeals]

74
00:04:29,447 --> 00:04:31,741
Let me know if anything starts hurting,
all right?

75
00:04:31,825 --> 00:04:33,243
[Anzu] Okay, thanks.

76
00:04:34,494 --> 00:04:36,496
[sighs]
This is so incredibly unfair,

77
00:04:36,579 --> 00:04:37,539
I can't even…

78
00:04:37,622 --> 00:04:40,667
Both of those heartthrobs are just
so worried about you.

79
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:44,045
Well, actually,
Kazuki wasn't worried about me at all.

80
00:04:47,048 --> 00:04:49,968
A FEW DAYS LATER.

81
00:04:50,969 --> 00:04:52,929
[Anzu] Maybe I'm a little early.

82
00:04:56,057 --> 00:04:59,060
[Tsuchiya] Would this coming Saturday
work for you?

83
00:05:00,228 --> 00:05:02,355
[Anzu] What else is left to go over?

84
00:05:02,439 --> 00:05:04,482
[car approaching]

85
00:05:07,319 --> 00:05:09,487
[Hijiri scoffs]
You're extremely early.

86
00:05:10,864 --> 00:05:13,992
You wanted to see me so bad
you've been waiting here since last night?

87
00:05:15,535 --> 00:05:17,996
You really are something else, aren't you?

88
00:05:18,079 --> 00:05:20,874
[forced laugh]
Oh yeah, I've been waiting all night.

89
00:05:20,957 --> 00:05:23,501
Held strong,
like I was defending the Alamo.

90
00:05:24,502 --> 00:05:25,837
Whatever.

91
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:28,214
What's with the peasant look
you've got on?

92
00:05:28,298 --> 00:05:30,884
[Hijiri] How could you even stand
next to me dressed like that?

93
00:05:30,967 --> 00:05:32,302
Are you trying to insult me?

94
00:05:32,385 --> 00:05:34,763
-[angry meow]
-[grunts]

95
00:05:35,764 --> 00:05:39,392
[Anzu] I humbly apologize.
I'm just a low-born villager NPC

96
00:05:39,476 --> 00:05:41,853
in a game, repeating the same line
over and over again.

97
00:05:41,936 --> 00:05:42,771
VILLAGER A

98
00:05:43,354 --> 00:05:45,398
[scoffs]
Whatever.

99
00:05:46,107 --> 00:05:47,025
-[Hijiri] Get in.
-Huh?

100
00:05:47,108 --> 00:05:48,401
[yelps]

101
00:05:48,485 --> 00:05:50,028
[groans]

102
00:05:50,111 --> 00:05:53,031
-You lack sincerity.
-[growls]

103
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:57,535
With all my attention,
you'll be our school's Cinderella.

104
00:05:58,620 --> 00:06:01,790
[Anzu] Wanted:
Someone to translate for this guy.

105
00:06:04,876 --> 00:06:05,960
[Anzu] Well…

106
00:06:06,878 --> 00:06:09,589
[magical music]

107
00:06:14,010 --> 00:06:17,889
-What the heck am I doing here?
-Aah…

108
00:06:18,765 --> 00:06:20,892
Hmm. Now you're decent.

109
00:06:21,392 --> 00:06:23,812
And now I wanna know what's happening.

110
00:06:25,897 --> 00:06:28,024
-Get her some flat shoes.
-[approaching footsteps]

111
00:06:28,108 --> 00:06:29,692
[Hijiri] Why are you unnecessarily tall?

112
00:06:29,776 --> 00:06:32,153
Maybe I should give you
some of my height, then.

113
00:06:34,364 --> 00:06:37,117
-[Hijiri] Okay, let's go to lunch.
-Huh? Whoa, wait, what?

114
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:39,244
Go to lunch, why?

115
00:06:41,079 --> 00:06:43,164
[Hijiri] I'm really pushed for time here.

116
00:06:43,248 --> 00:06:45,667
-Tell me what's going on!
-We're doing French.

117
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:48,169
[groans]
I don't need lunch!

118
00:06:49,254 --> 00:06:52,799
I don't get why you think it's okay
to make me over like that!

119
00:06:53,383 --> 00:06:54,843
It's entirely your fault

120
00:06:55,426 --> 00:06:58,304
for showing up on a date with me
dressed like a poor being.

121
00:06:58,888 --> 00:07:00,557
What are you talking about, date?

122
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:03,017
Aren't we meeting 'cause I got hit?

123
00:07:03,101 --> 00:07:04,227
No need to play dumb.

124
00:07:04,853 --> 00:07:07,856
You purposefully got hit
in order to get closer to me, right?

125
00:07:08,398 --> 00:07:09,649
Huh?

126
00:07:11,985 --> 00:07:14,863
Cars are legally at fault
when they hit pedestrians.

127
00:07:14,946 --> 00:07:18,324
You took advantage of that
so you could go out with me, didn't you?

128
00:07:18,408 --> 00:07:21,119
You actually think
that I staged the accident?

129
00:07:21,202 --> 00:07:23,705
-Oh, did you not?
-Not at all, no!

130
00:07:23,788 --> 00:07:25,457
Idiots like that exist?

131
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:28,001
It's happened countless times
since preschool.

132
00:07:28,084 --> 00:07:29,502
So several exist, then.

133
00:07:29,586 --> 00:07:32,338
Tsuchiya's driver's license is
on a permanent watchlist now.

134
00:07:32,422 --> 00:07:33,882
[Tsuchiya] It was suspended once too.

135
00:07:33,965 --> 00:07:36,885
[Anzu] You poor thing.
I'm really, really sorry!

136
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:40,597
Anyway, I'm not one of those girls, and I,

137
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:42,724
I can't accept these clothes.

138
00:07:42,807 --> 00:07:43,892
I'll pay for them.

139
00:07:44,392 --> 00:07:46,728
Nine hundred dollars, just for the dress.

140
00:07:46,811 --> 00:07:47,645
[yelps]

141
00:07:47,729 --> 00:07:49,647
Is it made out of an ancient relic silk
or something?

142
00:07:49,731 --> 00:07:50,815
YOU OBTAINED ANCIENT THREADS!

143
00:07:50,899 --> 00:07:52,233
Whatever.

144
00:07:52,317 --> 00:07:55,278
Intentional or no,
it was still an accident.

145
00:07:56,404 --> 00:07:59,699
You received clothes and you're also
about to have lunch with me.

146
00:08:00,283 --> 00:08:02,452
Think of it as a peasant's godsend.

147
00:08:03,411 --> 00:08:05,330
[groaning]

148
00:08:06,331 --> 00:08:07,916
[Anzu] Mr. Tsuchiya, please stop.

149
00:08:10,418 --> 00:08:11,628
What now?

150
00:08:11,711 --> 00:08:13,922
I feel bad
that you did all of this for me.

151
00:08:14,422 --> 00:08:17,342
-Whoa? Huh?
-[accessories jingle]

152
00:08:18,176 --> 00:08:20,470
I'm not at all interested in you.

153
00:08:20,553 --> 00:08:21,596
[gasps]

154
00:08:21,679 --> 00:08:24,307
[Anzu] So there's no need for us
to waste each other's time.

155
00:08:25,683 --> 00:08:26,643
See ya.

156
00:08:28,102 --> 00:08:29,479
[retreating footsteps]

157
00:08:29,562 --> 00:08:33,191
[Anzu] Being manipulated
by an extremely full of himself rich kid

158
00:08:33,274 --> 00:08:34,108
is really annoying,

159
00:08:34,192 --> 00:08:37,278
especially when he's got
a stuck-up attitude like that.

160
00:08:37,362 --> 00:08:39,489
But the most frustrating thing is

161
00:08:40,198 --> 00:08:43,243
he actually thought
I was one of those idiots

162
00:08:43,326 --> 00:08:45,870
who would stage an accident for a date!

163
00:08:45,954 --> 00:08:47,622
[men laughing]

164
00:08:47,705 --> 00:08:51,209
[Anzu in deep voice] I belong
to a warrior race that forges its way down

165
00:08:51,292 --> 00:08:54,295
the exact opposite path of life
every single day!

166
00:08:55,088 --> 00:08:57,507
[screams, heavy breathing]

167
00:08:57,590 --> 00:09:01,135
[Anzu] Damn, my pits are sweating
all over this 900-dollar dress.

168
00:09:01,219 --> 00:09:03,638
THIS IS A ROMANTIC ANIME

169
00:09:05,723 --> 00:09:09,352
She has no interest in me?

170
00:09:10,478 --> 00:09:13,398
[birds chirping]

171
00:09:15,483 --> 00:09:17,026
HIJIRI LOVE

172
00:09:17,110 --> 00:09:19,779
-That's not good. Mr. Hijiri looks sad.
-[girls swooning]

173
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:22,490
But he looks so fragile and beautiful.

174
00:09:23,533 --> 00:09:24,993
[approaching footsteps]

175
00:09:25,076 --> 00:09:25,910
Huh?

176
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:28,538
Hijiri Koganei.

177
00:09:28,621 --> 00:09:31,165
Uh, it's you.

178
00:09:31,749 --> 00:09:34,502
Address me respectfully. That was rude.

179
00:09:34,586 --> 00:09:36,796
[sighs]
Are you kidding me?

180
00:09:36,879 --> 00:09:39,841
[scoffs]
What do you want anyway?

181
00:09:39,924 --> 00:09:42,385
Trying to make up
for being rude the other day?

182
00:09:42,468 --> 00:09:45,513
[Anzu] I dry-cleaned the clothes,
so I just wanted to return them to you.

183
00:09:45,597 --> 00:09:46,598
Goodbye.

184
00:09:46,681 --> 00:09:47,807
[retreating footsteps]

185
00:09:51,561 --> 00:09:53,438
[Hijiri] She certainly left in a hurry

186
00:09:53,521 --> 00:09:56,482
after going out of her way
to return the gifts I gave her.

187
00:09:58,526 --> 00:10:01,195
There's no need
to worry about that peasant.

188
00:10:01,779 --> 00:10:04,782
But the way she's been giving me
all of that attitude…

189
00:10:05,450 --> 00:10:07,452
[sinister music]

190
00:10:07,535 --> 00:10:08,911
[Hijiri] I don't like it one bit.

191
00:10:11,247 --> 00:10:14,042
Tsuchiya, I need something investigated.

192
00:10:14,125 --> 00:10:16,127
[cheerful music]

193
00:10:17,128 --> 00:10:19,005
[Junta humming]

194
00:10:19,589 --> 00:10:21,591
Junta, you're chipper.

195
00:10:21,674 --> 00:10:24,594
Wednesday means no club,
so I get to walk home with you.

196
00:10:24,677 --> 00:10:26,346
Oh, okay, I see.

197
00:10:26,429 --> 00:10:28,181
Kazuki has work today, right?

198
00:10:28,264 --> 00:10:30,516
Yeah. What should we do for dinner?

199
00:10:31,517 --> 00:10:34,103
It might be terrible,
but I can make us something.

200
00:10:34,604 --> 00:10:36,606
Really? You would? I'll eat it!

201
00:10:38,191 --> 00:10:40,652
You know, maybe I should learn
how to cook myself.

202
00:10:40,735 --> 00:10:42,487
I only know how to make ramen.

203
00:10:42,987 --> 00:10:44,989
You should just focus on your baseball.

204
00:10:45,615 --> 00:10:48,326
[Anzu] He's such a good guy
compared to that other one.

205
00:10:48,409 --> 00:10:52,205
I hope Junta finds happiness
with someone he truly loves.

206
00:10:52,288 --> 00:10:55,792
But for that to happen,
I really need to do something about them.

207
00:10:55,875 --> 00:10:57,001
-[Riri] Anzu!
-[blows air]

208
00:10:57,585 --> 00:11:00,088
I wanna come too! Can I come for dinner?

209
00:11:00,171 --> 00:11:02,006
[Anzu] Maybe I should just give her
a quick death.

210
00:11:02,090 --> 00:11:03,508
[Anzu] Honestly, how dare you?

211
00:11:04,092 --> 00:11:06,302
Why send such a ridiculous character?

212
00:11:06,386 --> 00:11:08,096
There's no way I'd fall for him!

213
00:11:08,179 --> 00:11:11,516
Oh, when I'm in this form,
everybody can see and hear us.

214
00:11:11,599 --> 00:11:12,517
[giggles]

215
00:11:13,643 --> 00:11:17,188
Well, I'm not a very good cook,
so you should probably just go home.

216
00:11:17,271 --> 00:11:19,524
-Not letting go of that grip, then?
-Hmm?

217
00:11:21,692 --> 00:11:22,527
[Junta] Uh…

218
00:11:22,610 --> 00:11:24,112
-[car door opens]
-[both] Huh?

219
00:11:25,196 --> 00:11:26,531
Anzu Hoshino.

220
00:11:27,115 --> 00:11:28,157
-Not him.
-[chuckles]

221
00:11:28,741 --> 00:11:32,161
You're the first woman to say
that you have no interest in me at all.

222
00:11:32,995 --> 00:11:34,163
I'm intrigued.

223
00:11:35,081 --> 00:11:37,917
Just know
that I'll steal your heart eventually.

224
00:11:38,709 --> 00:11:40,837
-Heh.
-[squeals]

225
00:11:44,298 --> 00:11:46,217
-Aren't you starving?
-Mm-hm.

226
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:49,220
-[Riri] Oh, jeez. My stomach just rumbled…
-Goodness. Such a cramped place.

227
00:11:49,303 --> 00:11:52,473
-Oh! So, Junta…
-I'm sure it is for you, Mr. Prince.

228
00:11:52,557 --> 00:11:54,851
-[Hijiri] By the way, who are these two?
-[both] Huh?

229
00:11:54,934 --> 00:11:57,019
[Hijiri] My business is only with Hoshino.

230
00:11:57,103 --> 00:11:57,937
[Junta sighs]

231
00:11:58,729 --> 00:12:00,606
I'm Riri, Anzu's cousin.

232
00:12:01,107 --> 00:12:04,360
And this is one of her oldest friends
from childhood, Junta.

233
00:12:04,444 --> 00:12:07,613
The three of us will be having dinner
together tonight.

234
00:12:07,697 --> 00:12:09,449
You can actually leave now.

235
00:12:10,283 --> 00:12:11,451
So…

236
00:12:12,034 --> 00:12:14,704
What's this business?
Some more lame stuff?

237
00:12:15,538 --> 00:12:17,039
[Hijiri] Tsuchiya.

238
00:12:17,123 --> 00:12:17,999
Yes, sir.

239
00:12:20,168 --> 00:12:22,962
-Huh? Hmm…
-Miss Hoshino, this is for you.

240
00:12:25,548 --> 00:12:26,466
[Anzu] Huh?

241
00:12:27,091 --> 00:12:29,469
[Anzu] It's a Skitch! And a VR headset!

242
00:12:30,219 --> 00:12:32,680
The chocolates are all fancy brands!

243
00:12:33,764 --> 00:12:36,100
[squealing]

244
00:12:36,184 --> 00:12:38,060
-[Tsuchiya] And that's not all, miss.
-Huh?

245
00:12:38,603 --> 00:12:39,979
[Anzu yelps]

246
00:12:40,062 --> 00:12:43,983
-[meowing]
-[Anzu whimpers]

247
00:12:49,071 --> 00:12:51,908
[Anzu] Destruction level: severe.

248
00:12:51,991 --> 00:12:52,992
[meowing]

249
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:56,996
Well, you appear
to be satisfied with my gifts.

250
00:12:57,079 --> 00:12:58,998
[Anzu] That came out of nowhere.

251
00:12:59,081 --> 00:13:02,585
Did he actually feel bad
about me getting upset?

252
00:13:03,085 --> 00:13:06,964
Along with great elegance
and my appearance which exudes charm,

253
00:13:08,090 --> 00:13:11,260
I have the financial power
to make your every wish come true.

254
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:13,596
[gasps]

255
00:13:13,679 --> 00:13:15,640
You're interested in me now, right?

256
00:13:15,723 --> 00:13:18,017
Oh, so it's that kind of scenario.

257
00:13:18,601 --> 00:13:21,479
Tell me, how did you find out
about my favorite things?

258
00:13:21,562 --> 00:13:23,231
Anything's possible for me.

259
00:13:23,314 --> 00:13:24,899
No, an actual answer.

260
00:13:26,484 --> 00:13:30,321
[Anzu] It really bothered you when I said
I wasn't interested in you, didn't it?

261
00:13:31,113 --> 00:13:32,114
[Anzu grunts]

262
00:13:32,990 --> 00:13:35,034
-[in deep voice] Well, guess what? Hey!
-Stop right there!

263
00:13:35,117 --> 00:13:38,538
Anzu, hon, I just need
a quick word with you for a second!

264
00:13:41,624 --> 00:13:45,294
I know that we confiscated
your three greatest desires,

265
00:13:45,378 --> 00:13:48,548
but it would be very rude
of you to reject his gifts.

266
00:13:48,631 --> 00:13:50,925
I will allow 'em,

267
00:13:51,008 --> 00:13:53,553
but here's the catch for accepting them!

268
00:13:53,636 --> 00:13:55,263
What, are you serious?

269
00:13:55,346 --> 00:13:56,556
You can only keep 'em

270
00:13:56,639 --> 00:14:00,017
if you allow a relationship
to develop with Hijiri Koganei.

271
00:14:00,643 --> 00:14:01,561
[sighs]

272
00:14:04,897 --> 00:14:06,941
-[Anzu] If I start dating him…
-[arrogant laughter]

273
00:14:08,150 --> 00:14:11,237
…I can enjoy all those gifts right now.

274
00:14:12,113 --> 00:14:14,365
[kittens meowing]

275
00:14:16,742 --> 00:14:19,245
What are those two
talking about out there?

276
00:14:19,328 --> 00:14:21,038
Who… who knows?

277
00:14:21,873 --> 00:14:22,999
[sighs]

278
00:14:23,082 --> 00:14:26,043
Um, your name was Koganei?

279
00:14:26,127 --> 00:14:27,628
That's informal and rude.

280
00:14:27,712 --> 00:14:30,506
Oh, sorry, Mr. Koganei.

281
00:14:30,590 --> 00:14:33,759
I heard about the accident
with Anzu and everything.

282
00:14:34,844 --> 00:14:37,013
But, um, well, do you, um…

283
00:14:37,930 --> 00:14:41,017
[Junta] Anzu, uh, do you like her?

284
00:14:43,603 --> 00:14:44,604
Like her?

285
00:14:46,022 --> 00:14:49,025
That's not an emotion
I'd feel for anyone at all.

286
00:14:49,692 --> 00:14:52,528
That's an emotion
everyone else feels for me.

287
00:14:53,362 --> 00:14:54,530
Right.

288
00:14:54,614 --> 00:14:58,284
But Hoshino's stated
that she has absolutely no interest in me.

289
00:14:59,076 --> 00:15:00,453
It's a serious matter.

290
00:15:00,536 --> 00:15:03,539
[Junta] I see.
That's why you're doing all this.

291
00:15:05,124 --> 00:15:08,920
Just so you know, Anzu won't become
your friend just because…

292
00:15:09,670 --> 00:15:11,505
you're rich or you're good-looking.

293
00:15:13,132 --> 00:15:14,008
Hmm?

294
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:16,052
[slaps]

295
00:15:16,135 --> 00:15:19,472
[Anzu] You're completely clueless
about humans.

296
00:15:20,139 --> 00:15:23,726
Setting up forced encounters
and messing with emotions,

297
00:15:23,809 --> 00:15:26,062
now luring me in with my desires.

298
00:15:29,315 --> 00:15:30,441
I'm no fool.

299
00:15:33,110 --> 00:15:33,945
Oh.

300
00:15:34,779 --> 00:15:37,949
-Please leave. I don't want this stuff.
-How could…

301
00:15:38,032 --> 00:15:40,952
[Anzu] I'm incredibly sorry
if I hurt your pride,

302
00:15:41,535 --> 00:15:43,955
but you'll have to find someone else
to fawn over you.

303
00:15:44,622 --> 00:15:48,501
And since you're human,
you understand feelings.

304
00:15:48,584 --> 00:15:49,543
Right, Hijiri?

305
00:15:50,544 --> 00:15:53,089
[Anzu] And another thing,
there's no point strutting around

306
00:15:53,172 --> 00:15:55,257
promising my every wish
with your parents' money.

307
00:15:55,341 --> 00:15:57,760
It's okay when it's money
you earn yourself.

308
00:15:59,679 --> 00:16:00,972
And above all…

309
00:16:03,099 --> 00:16:05,977
If you don't have Momohiki,
then you don't have a chance!

310
00:16:09,063 --> 00:16:09,981
[sighs]

311
00:16:11,107 --> 00:16:12,066
[exhales sharply]

312
00:16:13,567 --> 00:16:16,070
[huffs, sighs]

313
00:16:20,741 --> 00:16:22,493
That was interesting.

314
00:16:23,786 --> 00:16:25,121
Junta…

315
00:16:25,204 --> 00:16:27,790
[Anzu]
If I had accepted Riri's conditions,

316
00:16:27,873 --> 00:16:30,960
would they have released Junta
from the love spell?

317
00:16:31,043 --> 00:16:32,336
[exhales sharply]

318
00:16:33,295 --> 00:16:35,047
I'm sorry you're involved with this.

319
00:16:35,631 --> 00:16:37,508
Don't be. I'm just fine.

320
00:16:38,843 --> 00:16:41,512
If you're ever in trouble,
please just let me know.

321
00:16:43,556 --> 00:16:44,515
[whimpers]

322
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:48,019
[Anzu] He's too good of a person
it's painful.

323
00:16:49,395 --> 00:16:50,521
[chuckles]

324
00:16:51,897 --> 00:16:54,900
Hey Anzu, how come
you're playing with him anyway?

325
00:16:55,526 --> 00:16:57,611
Yeah, I won't let you play my new game.

326
00:16:59,071 --> 00:17:01,032
What? You suck.

327
00:17:01,115 --> 00:17:05,619
-[Junta] Uh, are you sure?
-It's okay. Those guys are all talk.

328
00:17:07,038 --> 00:17:09,290
And I had plans to hang with you first.

329
00:17:10,624 --> 00:17:12,793
How come you kicked him out, huh?

330
00:17:12,877 --> 00:17:14,545
I really want to kick you out.

331
00:17:14,628 --> 00:17:16,589
-[Riri] Not nice!
-[chuckles]

332
00:17:17,631 --> 00:17:19,383
DONUTS

333
00:17:19,467 --> 00:17:20,551
[rustling]

334
00:17:20,634 --> 00:17:21,927
[sighs]

335
00:17:22,011 --> 00:17:25,514
[manager] Miss Hoshino,
we've got a new employee starting today.

336
00:17:25,598 --> 00:17:26,724
Oh, right.

337
00:17:28,017 --> 00:17:28,934
[Anzu] What?

338
00:17:29,852 --> 00:17:31,103
[manager] This is Mr. Koganei.

339
00:17:31,187 --> 00:17:33,189
[bright music]

340
00:17:33,272 --> 00:17:35,983
Yes, I'm here to learn.
You should have no issues.

341
00:17:36,525 --> 00:17:38,444
CONBINI MART
SEASONAL SWEETS

342
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:40,404
Welcome in.

343
00:17:44,492 --> 00:17:45,951
I appreciate that.

344
00:17:48,204 --> 00:17:49,080
Come again.

345
00:17:49,663 --> 00:17:51,749
Hey!

346
00:17:51,832 --> 00:17:53,793
How many meters above us are you?

347
00:17:53,876 --> 00:17:55,753
Excuse you, millions of meters.

348
00:17:56,420 --> 00:17:57,755
Orbitally higher?

349
00:17:58,339 --> 00:18:00,299
You think that's good customer service?

350
00:18:00,925 --> 00:18:01,759
She's right.

351
00:18:02,551 --> 00:18:04,011
It's better if you add,

352
00:18:04,095 --> 00:18:07,264
"But I won't actually wait for you"
after "Come again."

353
00:18:07,348 --> 00:18:09,767
[Anzu]
Don't encourage the hot and cold thing!

354
00:18:11,018 --> 00:18:13,562
Manager, sir, are you sure about this?

355
00:18:13,646 --> 00:18:15,773
Hmm, well, thing is…

356
00:18:15,856 --> 00:18:16,816
[device beeps]

357
00:18:16,899 --> 00:18:19,151
-Shall I warm it?
-Oh, yes.

358
00:18:19,235 --> 00:18:22,488
[manager] The customers all seem
to be attracted to Mr. Koganei's aura,

359
00:18:22,571 --> 00:18:24,073
so there haven't been any complaints.

360
00:18:24,156 --> 00:18:26,784
[Anzu]
But he's inconsiderate and obnoxious!

361
00:18:28,702 --> 00:18:32,206
Hijiri went viral,
known as the convenience store prince.

362
00:18:32,289 --> 00:18:36,710
The #storeprince spread
like wildfire all over social media…

363
00:18:36,794 --> 00:18:38,254
SEASONAL SWEETS NOW AVAILABLE

364
00:18:38,337 --> 00:18:40,714
…and attracted a whole lot of customers!

365
00:18:40,798 --> 00:18:43,217
[customers whispering]

366
00:18:43,843 --> 00:18:45,177
Mm-hm.

367
00:18:46,303 --> 00:18:52,226
AVAILABLE NATIONWIDE

368
00:18:53,435 --> 00:18:55,229
Your change. Do come again.

369
00:18:55,312 --> 00:18:56,564
Thanks.

370
00:18:56,647 --> 00:18:57,690
[Anzu grumbles]

371
00:18:58,315 --> 00:19:00,651
[Anzu] I guess he must've ended up
with that attitude

372
00:19:00,734 --> 00:19:03,737
because everyone around him
seems to enable him.

373
00:19:04,446 --> 00:19:06,740
But he is a fast learner,

374
00:19:06,824 --> 00:19:09,076
and he doesn't ask for time off.

375
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:11,495
-And to be honest, he does work hard.
-Welcome in.

376
00:19:13,455 --> 00:19:15,332
-You can take your break now.
-Mm-hm.

377
00:19:15,833 --> 00:19:17,168
[chuckles]

378
00:19:17,251 --> 00:19:19,253
Wait, is the Prince going on break?

379
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:22,256
Sorry about that.
[chuckles awkwardly]

380
00:19:22,339 --> 00:19:25,259
CONBINI MART

381
00:19:26,844 --> 00:19:29,763
[moans]
I'm so tired.

382
00:19:29,847 --> 00:19:32,016
Oh, Mr. Tsuchiya.

383
00:19:34,602 --> 00:19:35,895
Good evening, miss.

384
00:19:35,978 --> 00:19:38,397
Hi there. Hijiri will be out in a sec.

385
00:19:41,066 --> 00:19:42,026
Miss Hoshino.

386
00:19:42,526 --> 00:19:46,113
I don't know how to express the gratitude
I have for what you have done.

387
00:19:46,780 --> 00:19:47,781
What?

388
00:19:48,949 --> 00:19:53,537
Mr. Hijiri, he attended an expensive
escalator-styled private school,

389
00:19:53,621 --> 00:19:55,039
but due to his father's wishes,

390
00:19:55,122 --> 00:19:57,791
he was enrolled at the school
where you currently attend.

391
00:19:57,875 --> 00:19:59,043
Oh.

392
00:19:59,126 --> 00:20:00,961
[Tsuchiya] His loved ones
are enamored with him,

393
00:20:01,045 --> 00:20:04,215
and he always got anything
and everything he wanted growing up,

394
00:20:04,298 --> 00:20:06,884
so he can be a bit out of touch,
and he lacks common sense.

395
00:20:06,967 --> 00:20:07,801
Hmm…

396
00:20:08,594 --> 00:20:10,930
His father became concerned about that,

397
00:20:11,013 --> 00:20:13,098
so he decided that he wanted Hijiri

398
00:20:13,182 --> 00:20:15,768
to experience a normal life
at a normal school.

399
00:20:16,393 --> 00:20:19,271
[Tsuchiya] However, his innate
and inherent heir of nobility

400
00:20:19,355 --> 00:20:21,815
has always made him feel
above everything normal.

401
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:23,817
Right.

402
00:20:24,526 --> 00:20:28,405
But now, because you had the ability
to reason with him directly…

403
00:20:28,906 --> 00:20:32,326
First, I hit the bottom right key there.
And then I enter…

404
00:20:32,409 --> 00:20:37,248
[Tsuchiya] Mr. Hijiri has actually been
trying to learn more about normal life.

405
00:20:38,999 --> 00:20:40,584
This is all your doing.

406
00:20:41,126 --> 00:20:42,586
Thank you so very much.

407
00:20:42,670 --> 00:20:44,213
Oh, of course.

408
00:20:45,339 --> 00:20:46,590
[chuckles]

409
00:20:49,176 --> 00:20:51,595
NARIKIN BANK

410
00:20:51,679 --> 00:20:53,597
BANK ACCOUNT
ORDINARY FINANCIALS

411
00:20:53,681 --> 00:20:54,598
[squeals, gasps]

412
00:20:55,182 --> 00:20:56,558
My paycheck!

413
00:20:57,142 --> 00:21:00,437
I'm so glad. How should I spend it? Hmm…

414
00:21:00,521 --> 00:21:02,314
[chuckles]

415
00:21:02,398 --> 00:21:04,233
-[Hijiri] Hoshino.
-[gasps]

416
00:21:05,276 --> 00:21:06,318
[shrieks]

417
00:21:07,027 --> 00:21:10,072
Jeez, Hijiri!
There's no work today, is there?

418
00:21:10,155 --> 00:21:11,782
Then why are you following me?

419
00:21:11,865 --> 00:21:15,327
How rude. I just happened to see you
so I called your name.

420
00:21:16,036 --> 00:21:17,830
I received my paycheck today.

421
00:21:17,913 --> 00:21:20,541
So, Hoshino, what do you want?

422
00:21:21,125 --> 00:21:22,042
Huh?

423
00:21:22,126 --> 00:21:24,837
It's only a few days' worth
so it can't be too great,

424
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:27,548
but I'm sure I can fulfill anything
your peasant heart desires.

425
00:21:28,549 --> 00:21:30,551
And I earned the money all on my own.

426
00:21:31,510 --> 00:21:33,554
But don't get the wrong idea.

427
00:21:33,637 --> 00:21:35,097
[Hijiri chuckles dryly]

428
00:21:37,391 --> 00:21:39,852
It's not like
I did any of this stuff for you.

429
00:21:40,561 --> 00:21:43,439
[Anzu] That hot and cold personality
was implanted in him.

430
00:21:44,106 --> 00:21:45,107
What do you want?

431
00:21:45,190 --> 00:21:48,277
-A bag? Some shoes?
-No, no, thanks.

432
00:21:48,360 --> 00:21:50,612
-Some jewelry?
-No, no, no, no.

433
00:21:50,696 --> 00:21:52,489
Instead of a gift,
would you prefer a date?

434
00:21:52,573 --> 00:21:53,449
Please, shut up!

435
00:21:53,532 --> 00:21:56,869
[Anzu] As much as I want to say
I don't want a thing from him…

436
00:21:56,952 --> 00:21:59,455
[soft piano music]

437
00:22:02,708 --> 00:22:04,126
Hmm.

438
00:22:04,209 --> 00:22:07,379
Oh! All right, I know what I want.

439
00:22:10,841 --> 00:22:11,925
[Anzu chuckles]

440
00:22:13,469 --> 00:22:14,970
What in the world is that?

441
00:22:15,054 --> 00:22:16,972
Pipiko. You wouldn't know.

442
00:22:18,140 --> 00:22:20,934
It was surprisingly cheap,
even for a peasant's item.

443
00:22:21,018 --> 00:22:22,394
-[snaps]
-Hmm?

444
00:22:23,312 --> 00:22:24,897
[Anzu] Here. That's your half.

445
00:22:28,108 --> 00:22:29,902
Thank you for the treat.
[chuckles]

446
00:22:30,736 --> 00:22:32,488
You're happy with something like this?

447
00:22:33,489 --> 00:22:36,492
Well yeah, I think it's the perfect thing
to share with friends.

448
00:22:36,992 --> 00:22:38,077
[exclaims]

449
00:22:44,792 --> 00:22:45,751
What do you think?

450
00:22:47,211 --> 00:22:49,338
It tastes artificial and cheap.

451
00:22:51,131 --> 00:22:53,050
But it's, it's not bad.

452
00:22:53,133 --> 00:22:55,385
[magical music]

453
00:22:56,011 --> 00:22:56,887
[gasps]

454
00:22:57,763 --> 00:22:59,306
[yelps, grunts]

455
00:22:59,973 --> 00:23:00,808
What's wrong?

456
00:23:01,391 --> 00:23:03,811
Getting back my sanity. That's all.

457
00:23:04,895 --> 00:23:05,813
[Anzu grunts]

458
00:23:07,356 --> 00:23:09,441
[Anzu]
This might have been a huge mistake.

459
00:23:11,401 --> 00:23:13,320
[scrubbing]

460
00:23:16,406 --> 00:23:17,908
[door opens]

461
00:23:19,827 --> 00:23:22,162
I'm home, guys.

462
00:23:23,163 --> 00:23:24,331
[phone chimes, vibrates]

463
00:23:25,916 --> 00:23:26,917
What?

464
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:27,835
ARISA
CAN WE MEET?

465
00:23:27,918 --> 00:23:28,961
[Anzu] It's Kazuki's phone.

466
00:23:29,044 --> 00:23:30,337
ARISA
CAN WE MEET?

467
00:23:30,420 --> 00:23:34,341
[Anzu gasps]
It's a girl!

468
00:23:36,802 --> 00:23:38,554
A fanfare, please!

469
00:23:38,637 --> 00:23:40,639
And a big congratulations!

470
00:23:40,722 --> 00:23:43,016
Did you fall for my little trick?

471
00:23:43,100 --> 00:23:46,061
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

472
00:23:46,145 --> 00:23:49,815
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

473
00:23:49,898 --> 00:23:52,568
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

474
00:23:52,651 --> 00:23:54,945
[sighs]
Don't just let things be! Come on!

475
00:23:55,028 --> 00:23:57,698
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

476
00:23:57,781 --> 00:23:59,616
So I can make sure I get paid.

477
00:23:59,700 --> 00:24:01,869
[closing theme music]

478
00:24:01,952 --> 00:24:02,786
♪ Ah, yeah! ♪

479
00:24:05,289 --> 00:24:06,248
♪ Let's go! ♪

480
00:24:08,667 --> 00:24:09,793
♪ Lo-love! ♪

481
00:24:11,879 --> 00:24:12,838
♪ Here we go! ♪

482
00:00:01,695 --> 00:00:05,365
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

483
00:00:05,448 --> 00:00:08,118
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

484
00:00:08,201 --> 00:00:10,495
[sighs]
Don't just let things be! Come on!

485
00:00:10,578 --> 00:00:13,248
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

486
00:00:13,331 --> 00:00:15,166
So I can make sure I get paid.

487
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,419
[closing theme music]

488
00:00:17,502 --> 00:00:18,336
♪ Ah, yeah! ♪

489
00:00:20,839 --> 00:00:21,798
♪ Let's go! ♪

490
00:00:24,217 --> 00:00:25,343
♪ Lo-love! ♪

491
00:00:27,429 --> 00:00:28,388
♪ Here we go! ♪

